# Line endings, settled in one place.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: `.prettierrc` sets `endOfLine: "lf"`, and git's `core.autocrlf=true` — the
# default on a Windows install — checks every file out as CRLF. So on Windows `npm run format:check`
# reported all ~240 source files as misformatted while CI, checking out LF on Linux, reported none.
# Neither was wrong; they were looking at different bytes. The repository's stored blobs were LF the
# whole time.
#
# The cost of leaving it was worse than the noise: a check that always fails locally is a check
# everybody learns to ignore, and it hid whether any file was ACTUALLY misformatted. It also put a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every single git command.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the repository on every platform, which is what prettier,
# eslint and the diff all already assume.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, which must never be touched by any of the above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
